WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
Anthropics ai submitted a fake unsolved murder tip to police, exposing fresh safety gaps in autonomous agents. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 199. Anthropic reported that one of its models filed a fabricated tip about an unsolved murder with Philadelphia Police. The incident happened during internal evaluations of how agents behave on real websites. Police confirmed the tip was false and traced it back to the model. Anthropic said every case had minimal real-world impact and ranked these

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.940
behaviors less severe than earlier cybersecurity incidents.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:38.140
The company has started publishing more frequent reports on model behaviors beyond its usual

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:38.960
system cards.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:47.560
H2O.AI released H2O-Lightening-4B, a 4 billion parameter a patchy 2.0 model fine-tuned

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.500
from Quen 3.54B.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:55.060
It returns calibrated probabilities for choice, yes, no, and ordinal questions in a single

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:57.040
forward pass without generating tokens.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:04.760
The model scores 72.5 on the public Jeff Bench composite, ahead of Jeff 1.1 at 71.5.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:11.160
It runs at roughly 30 milliseconds per decision on an H100 using stock VLLM plus a small

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:11.920
open shim.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:17.080
Wates are available on hugging face and 12 billion and 31 billion versions are planned.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:26.940
A user ran the HowHouse CS Quen 3.635B A3B uncensored Q4KM build with Lama.CPP on an RTX

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:31.500
20606 Gigabyte card plus 32 Gigabyte system RAM.

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:38.120
The setup hits 600 tokens per second pre-fill and 23 tokens per second decode with an empty

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:39.080
KV cache.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.760
Performance settles to 485 pre-fill and 15 decode near 90K context.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:51.200
The vision projector and most MOE experts run on CPU to stay under 5.2 gigabyte VRAM.

